# Supabase project credentials consumed by both apps via createAlthaqalaynClient({ url, key }).
# The two apps expose env under different prefixes — copy these into each app's env:
#   apps/mobile (Expo):   EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL / EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
#   apps/admin  (Next.js): NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL / NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
#
# The anon key is safe to ship to clients — RLS (see src/schema.sql) distinguishes
# anon (public, published-only reads) from an authenticated admin session.
# NEVER put the service-role key in a client app.

SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
